          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What safety standards must OEM chargers meet for US and EU markets?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "US: UL 62368-1 (safety for AV/IT equipment), FCC (EMI). Most US retailers (Amazon, Walmart, Best Buy) require UL certification, products without it face delisting. EU: CE marking via EN 62368-1 (harmonized with IEC 62368-1) under the Low Voltage Directive, plus RoHS and ESPR 2025/2052 (≤0.1W standby, ≥87% active efficiency). Key difference: CE uses manufacturer self-declaration with a Technical File; UL requires NRTL testing plus quarterly factory follow-up inspections (~$1,500-3,000/year). GaN chargers require the same certifications plus additional thermal testing. WOWOHCOOL implements 10-layer circuit protection and UL 94 V-0 enclosures rated to 850°C glow wire across all products."
