          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "UL 62368-1 is the US safety standard for chargers and power adapters based on IEC 62368-1. It covers protection against electric shock, fire, thermal runaway, mechanical hazards, and radiation. The 4th Edition (published July 2025, mandatory February 15, 2027) is a major update: all components must now be certified to IEC 62368-1 (components under older IEC 60950-1/60065 are no longer accepted), adds dual-sensor thermal derating requirements, stricter thin-wall enclosure testing, and new single-fault analysis documentation. New OEM designs should target 4th Edition immediately to avoid re-certification costs in 2027."
          }
        },
