          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What are the risks of uncertified chargers for OEM brands and importers?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, the US CPSC recalled over 447,000 chargers (2025-2026) linked to fire and burn hazards, with 112 incidents and 1 fatality. Cheap chargers skip critical protection layers: over-voltage protection (OVP), over-current protection (OCP), over-temperature protection (OTP), and use non-V-0 plastics that ignite under fault conditions. Thermal runaway in lithium batteries can reach 800°C within seconds when internal temps exceed ~150°C. Prevention requires NTC temperature sensors, MCU-controlled charge cutoff, and dual-sensor thermal derating per IEC 62368-1 Ed.3. The cost of one recall far exceeds a product line's lifetime savings from cutting safety corners."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What safety testing should a quality charger factory perform on every unit?",
