            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Five verification steps: (1) Verify UL file number at iq.ulprospector.com, the product must appear as 'UL Listed' (not 'UL tested' or 'meets UL standards'). (2) Check FCC ID at fccid.io, confirm grantee name matches the factory. (3) Demand full test reports (30-80 pages) from ISO 17025-accredited labs (TÜV, SGS, Intertek, UL), not just 1-page certificates. (4) Verify the test report covers your exact model number, wattage, and plug version. (5) Check the CE Declaration of Conformity is in the importer's name, not the factory's. Red flags: PDF-only certificates with no online database entry, 'family' certificates without your SKU, test reports from unknown labs."
          }
