            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "UL certification: quarterly factory follow-up inspections (~$1,500-3,000/year) plus annual recertification audits. CE marking: updated Declaration of Conformity required when product design or applicable standards change, no fixed expiry but market surveillance can request documentation at any time. Major standard transitions (e.g., IEC 62368-1 Ed.3 to Ed.4, mandatory February 2027) require full re-testing and documentation updates. Technical files must be retained for 10 years after the last unit is sold (EU requirement). Non-compliance penalties: EU fines up to EUR 500,000, US FCC fines $16,000+ per violation per day, Amazon delisting, customs seizure without compensation."
