 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">The HBSE model is why modern standards require <strong>redundant</strong> safeguards: if one layer fails, a second must independently prevent the hazard from reaching the user. This "two-fault tolerance" philosophy runs through every section below.</p>

