 <!-- Section 3: IEC 62368-1 Testing Requirements for OEM Importers -->
 <section id="testing-requirements" class="mb-16">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">3. IEC 62368-1 Testing Checklist: 6 Tests Every OEM Importer Must Verify</h2>

 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">IEC 62368-1 compliance isn't a single test — it's a battery of electrical, mechanical, and thermal tests. For OEM importers, understanding these tests helps you verify that your supplier's certification is genuine and comprehensive. Below are the 6 core tests, what they mean, and the pass/fail criteria you should see in the test report.</p>

 <h3 class="font-black text-slate-900 uppercase mb-3">1. Dielectric Withstand (Hi-Pot) — Electrical Insulation</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">This test verifies that the insulation between primary (mains) and secondary (output) circuits can withstand high voltage without breaking down. A failure here means the charger can electrocute the user.</p>
 <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
 <table class="w-full text-sm text-left border-collapse">
 <thead><tr class="bg-slate-200"><th class="p-3 font-black text-slate-700 uppercase text-xs">Insulation Type</th><th class="p-3 font-black text-slate-700 uppercase text-xs">Test Voltage</th><th class="p-3 font-black text-slate-700 uppercase text-xs">Duration</th><th class="p-3 font-black text-slate-700 uppercase text-xs">Pass Criteria</th></tr></thead>
 <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200">
 <tr><td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-bold">Reinforced (Pri→Sec)</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">AC 3000V</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">60s</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">No breakdown or flashover</td></tr>
 <tr><td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-bold">Basic (Pri→GND)</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">AC 1500V</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">60s</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">Leakage &lt;5mA</td></tr>
 <tr><td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-bold">Class II (Double-Insulated)</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">AC 4000V</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">60s</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">No breakdown</td></tr>
 </tbody>
 </table>
 </div>

 <h3 class="font-black text-slate-900 uppercase mb-3">2. Temperature Rise — Thermal Safety at Full Load</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">Charger runs at <strong>100% rated load for 4+ hours</strong> at 40&deg;C ambient. Every accessible surface and internal component must stay within safe limits.</p>
 <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-slate-600 text-sm space-y-1 mb-4">
 <li><strong>External enclosure:</strong> Max 70&deg;C (metal), 85&deg;C (plastic TS1)</li>
 <li><strong>Internal transformer:</strong> Max 110&deg;C (Class B insulation), 130&deg;C (Class F)</li>
 <li><strong>Capacitors:</strong> Must operate within rated temperature range (typically 105&deg;C max)</li>
 <li><strong>Red flag:</strong> Report shows testing at 25&deg;C — invalid. Must be 40&deg;C ambient</li>
 </ul>

 <h3 class="font-black text-slate-900 uppercase mb-3">3. Single Fault Condition — What Happens When Something Breaks</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">IEC 62368-1 requires the charger to remain safe even when <strong>any single component fails</strong>. Common fault tests:</p>
 <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-slate-600 text-sm space-y-1 mb-4">
 <li><strong>Output short circuit:</strong> Charger must shut down safely (hiccup mode or latch-off), no fire or smoke</li>
 <li><strong>Optocoupler open:</strong> Feedback loop broken → output voltage must not exceed ES1 limits (60V DC)</li>
 <li><strong>Fan stall (if active cooled):</strong> Thermal protection must activate before unsafe temperatures</li>
 <li><strong>Overvoltage on input:</strong> 1.1× rated voltage for extended period — no damage</li>
 </ul>
 <div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 rounded-r-xl mb-4">
 <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm"><strong>Critical check:</strong> Ask your supplier for the single-fault test report specifically. Many factories skip this to save $1,000-2,000 in testing costs. A charger that passes normal operation but fails single-fault is dangerous.</p>
 </div>

 <h3 class="font-black text-slate-900 uppercase mb-3">4. Creepage &amp; Clearance — Physical Spacing on the PCB</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">This is the physical distance between high-voltage and low-voltage traces on the PCB. Insufficient spacing can cause arcing, especially in humid environments or at high altitude.</p>
 <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
 <table class="w-full text-sm text-left border-collapse">
 <thead><tr class="bg-slate-200"><th class="p-3 font-black text-slate-700 uppercase text-xs">Parameter</th><th class="p-3 font-black text-slate-700 uppercase text-xs">Reinforced Insulation</th><th class="p-3 font-black text-slate-700 uppercase text-xs">Basic Insulation</th></tr></thead>
 <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200">
 <tr><td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-bold">Creepage (along surface)</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">&ge;6.0mm (230V, PD2, Material Group III)</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">&ge;3.0mm</td></tr>
 <tr><td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-bold">Clearance (through air)</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">&ge;4.0mm</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">&ge;2.0mm</td></tr>
 <tr><td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-bold">Transformer margin tape</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600" colspan="2">3 layers minimum, &ge;0.05mm each</td></tr>
 </tbody>
 </table>
 </div>

 <h3 class="font-black text-slate-900 uppercase mb-3">5. Enclosure Mechanical — Drop, Impact &amp; Fire</h3>
 <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-slate-600 text-sm space-y-1 mb-4">
 <li><strong>Drop test:</strong> 3 drops from 1m onto hardwood — no safety hazard exposed, enclosure intact</li>
 <li><strong>Impact test:</strong> 0.5kg steel ball dropped from 1.3m — enclosure must not crack to expose live parts</li>
 <li><strong>Glow wire:</strong> 750&deg;C for fire enclosure (V-0/V-1 rated material required), 550&deg;C for non-fire enclosure</li>
 <li><strong>Ball pressure:</strong> 125&deg;C (external), 75&deg;C (internal) — deformation &lt;2mm diameter</li>
 </ul>

 <h3 class="font-black text-slate-900 uppercase mb-3">6. Safety-Critical Components — BOM Locked List</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">These components must be individually certified and cannot be substituted without re-testing. <strong>Any post-certification substitution voids the IEC 62368-1 certificate.</strong></p>
