 <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm">Across 200+ brand accounts, the three most common failure points we see are: <strong>(1) non-V-0 plastics</strong> that ignite during fault testing, <strong>(2) undersized Y-capacitors</strong> that fail dielectric strength tests, and <strong>(3) missing NTC on the secondary side</strong>, the charger has OTP on the primary but is blind to a hot USB-C connector. All three are invisible to the end user until a failure occurs.</p>
